  "TITLE": "How a Habit Becomes<br>Automatic",
  "LEAD": "A habit is a cue&ndash;routine&ndash;reward loop that, with repetition, shifts control from the deliberate prefrontal cortex to the basal ganglia, until the behavior runs without a decision. It works like a desire path across a lawn: every walker wears the groove a little deeper, and each new walker is more likely to take it &mdash; the way erosion carves a gully from a trickle.",
